# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. Everything here is optional.
# The GitHub Packages token for @thebensage-dev/ui goes in .npmrc instead (see .npmrc.example).

# The People API (the Api repo), which holds the data. Defaults to http://localhost:3002, the
# API's own `dotnet run` port. The local Docker stack (Infrastructure/local) runs one at
# http://api.localhost:8080, with the demo people.
# API_URL=http://localhost:3002

# Sign-in through authentik (OpenID Connect). Browsing is public; adding, editing and deleting
# need a signed-in user, whose access token the API checks. Leave these unset and the directory
# is read-only.
# The "user-directory" client is created by authentik's blueprint (Infrastructure/identity), which
# only admits the "user-directory-editors" group. Its callback is built from USER_DIRECTORY_URL
# there, which must equal APP_URL here; the secret must equal USER_DIRECTORY_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET.
# APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
# OIDC_ISSUER_URL=https://id.example.com/application/o/user-directory/
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=user-directory
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# At least 32 random characters (openssl rand -base64 32); encrypts the session cookie.
# AUTH_SECRET=
# Only when the server can't reach OIDC_ISSUER_URL itself: the origin to call instead (the local
# Docker stack sets http://authentik-server:9000).
# OIDC_INTERNAL_URL=

# Optional: the main site's URL (no trailing slash). Adds a footer with links to its privacy notice
# and terms (<MAIN_SITE_URL>/privacy and /terms). Left out when unset.
# MAIN_SITE_URL=https://example.com
